IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `act-ch8-commencement`

-- Tests for act-ch8-commencement.l4.
-- Every expected value is read from the section named beside the assertion, and was written before the run.

§ `Tests: chapter 8, Commencement`

-- s 72: law means an Act or statutory instrument; every kind of document in the Act's list is one or the other.
#ASSERT `s 72: the kind of document is a law for chapter 8` `an Act`
#ASSERT `s 72: the kind of document is a law for chapter 8` `a subordinate law`
#ASSERT `s 72: the kind of document is a law for chapter 8` `a statutory instrument of another kind`

-- s 73 (5): this section is subject to ss 75, 76, 79, 79A and 81.
#ASSERT `s 73 (5): the sections that s 73 is subject to` EQUALS LIST "75", "76", "79", "79A", "81"

-- s 75AA (1): applies if a law amends another law and includes a provision identifying the amended law.
#ASSERT `s 75AA (1): s 75AA applies to the law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 75AA (1): s 75AA applies to the law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 75AA (1): s 75AA applies to the law` FALSE TRUE)

-- s 75B (1): a law must not be taken to provide for retrospective commencement unless it clearly indicates it.
#ASSERT `s 75B (1): the law is taken to provide for the law (or another law) to commence retrospectively` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 75B (1): the law is taken to provide for the law (or another law) to commence retrospectively` FALSE)
-- s 75B (1) Example: the XYZ Act 2003 was notified on 1 July 2003 and says it is taken to have commenced on 17 October 2001; section 2 clearly indicates retrospective commencement.
#ASSERT `s 75B (1): the law is taken to provide for the law (or another law) to commence retrospectively` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75A (1): an Act or legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 1 7 2003) (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 17 10 2001))

-- s 76 (4): a prejudicial provision operates to the disadvantage of a person (other than the Territory or a territory authority or instrumentality) by adversely affecting rights or imposing liabilities.
#ASSERT `s 76 (4): the provision is a prejudicial provision` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76 (4): the provision is a prejudicial provision` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 76 (4): the provision is a prejudicial provision` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 76 (4): the provision is a prejudicial provision` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 76 (4): the provision is a non-prejudicial provision` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 76 (4): the provision is a non-prejudicial provision` TRUE)
-- s 76 (1): a statutory instrument may provide that a non-prejudicial provision commences retrospectively.
#ASSERT `s 76 (1): a statutory instrument may provide that the provision commences retrospectively` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76 (1): a statutory instrument may provide that the provision commences retrospectively` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 76 (2): unless displaced by or under authority given by an Act, a statutory instrument cannot provide that a prejudicial provision commences retrospectively.
#ASSERT `s 76 (2): a statutory instrument can provide that the prejudicial provision commences retrospectively` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76 (2): a statutory instrument can provide that the prejudicial provision commences retrospectively` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76 (2): a statutory instrument can provide that the prejudicial provision commences retrospectively` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 76 (2) Example: the Locust Damage Compensation Determination 2003 limits who can apply (adversely affecting rights); nothing authorises retrospective commencement;
-- the provision "cannot commence retrospectively" and commences on the day after the determination's notification day, 15 August 2003, that is 16 August 2003 (see s 73 (3)).
#ASSERT `s 76 (4): the provision is a prejudicial provision` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76 (2): a statutory instrument can provide that the prejudicial provision commences retrospectively` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` (Date 15 8 2003) (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2003))) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 16 8 2003)

-- s 77 (1): if a law is expressed to commence on a day fixed or otherwise determined by a notice, (a) a single day or time, or (b) different days or times for different provisions, may be fixed.
#ASSERT `s 77 (1) (a): a single day, or a time on a single day, may be fixed or determined` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 77 (1) (a): a single day, or a time on a single day, may be fixed or determined` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 77 (1) (b): different days or times may be fixed or determined for different provisions` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 77 (1) (b): different days or times may be fixed or determined for different provisions` FALSE)
-- s 77 (2): a commencement notice is valid even if the day or time fixed happens before the notice's notification day.
#ASSERT `s 77 (2): the commencement notice for the law is valid` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77 (2): the commencement notice for the law is valid` FALSE

-- s 78 (1): amendments made by a provision of a law may be given separate commencements.
#ASSERT `s 78 (1): the amendments may be given separate commencements` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 78 (1): the amendments may be given separate commencements` FALSE)
-- s 78 (1) Example 1: a provision of an amending law inserts 2 sections; the sections may be given separate commencements.
#ASSERT `s 78 (1), examples: the things inserted by the provision may be given separate commencements` "2 sections" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 78 (1) Example 2: a provision inserts a section divided into paragraphs; the paragraphs may be given separate commencements.
#ASSERT `s 78 (1), examples: the things inserted by the provision may be given separate commencements` "the paragraphs of a section divided into paragraphs" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78 (1), examples: the things inserted by the provision may be given separate commencements` "a whole Act" EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 79 (2): applies to a law unless displaced by an Act or, for a subordinate law or disallowable instrument, by the postponed law.
#ASSERT `s 79 (2): s 79 applies to the law` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79 (2): s 79 applies to the law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79 (2): s 79 applies to the law` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 79 (4): law means an Act, subordinate law, disallowable instrument or notifiable instrument.
#ASSERT `s 79 (4): the kind of document is a law for s 79` `an Act`
#ASSERT `s 79 (4): the kind of document is a law for s 79` `a subordinate law`
#ASSERT `s 79 (4): the kind of document is a law for s 79` `a disallowable instrument`
#ASSERT `s 79 (4): the kind of document is a law for s 79` `a notifiable instrument`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79 (4): the kind of document is a law for s 79` `a commencement notice`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79 (4): the kind of document is a law for s 79` `a statutory instrument of another kind`)
-- s 79 (4): notification day, for a postponed law: of the law, if it is a law; if it is a provision of a law, of the law that enacts the provision.
#ASSERT `s 79 (4): the notification day of the postponed law` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 9 9 2025) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 79 (4): the notification day of the postponed law` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 9 9 2025) EQUALS Date 9 9 2025
-- s 79 (4): postponed law means a law that does not commence on its notification day because a law postpones its commencement until a day or time fixed by a commencement notice.
#ASSERT `s 79 (4): the law is a postponed law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79 (4): the law is a postponed law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79 (4): the law is a postponed law` FALSE TRUE)

-- s 79A (1): applies if a law amends a law that has not commenced.
#ASSERT `s 79A (1): s 79A applies to the amending law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79A (1): s 79A applies to the amending law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 79A (1): s 79A applies to the amending law` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 79A (2): the amendment of the uncommenced law does not of itself commence that law.
#ASSERT `s 79A (2): the amendment of the uncommenced law of itself commences that law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 79A (2): the amendment of the uncommenced law of itself commences that law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 79A (3): the amendment commences on the commencement of the uncommenced law.
#ASSERT `s 79A (3): when the amendment made by the amending law commences` TRUE (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 9 2026)) EQUALS JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 9 2026))
#ASSERT `s 79A (3): when the amendment made by the amending law commences` FALSE (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 9 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 80 (a): a reference to the commencement of the law concerned, where its other provisions commence on a single day or at a single time, is the commencement of the remaining provisions.
#ASSERT `s 80: what a reference to the commencement of the law concerned is a reference to` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the commencement of the remaining provisions of the law concerned`
#ASSERT `s 80: what a reference to the commencement of the law concerned is a reference to` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the commencement of the remaining provisions of the law concerned`
-- (b): if (a) does not apply and the reference is in a provision of the law concerned, the commencement of that provision.
#ASSERT `s 80: what a reference to the commencement of the law concerned is a reference to` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the commencement of the provision containing the reference`
-- (c): in any other case, the commencement of the relevant provision of the law concerned.
#ASSERT `s 80: what a reference to the commencement of the law concerned is a reference to` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the commencement of the relevant provision of the law concerned`

-- s 81 (1): applies to a power given by a law that has been notified but not commenced, (b) or by a law as amended by another law, where the laws have been notified and any have not commenced.
#ASSERT `s 81 (1): s 81 applies to the power` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 81 (1): s 81 applies to the power` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 81 (1): s 81 applies to the power` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 81 (1) Examples—powers to which section applies: 1 power to delegate a function; 2 power to give or issue an approval, consent, licence, permit or other authority (however described); 3 power to make an acting appointment; 4 power to issue guidelines.
#ASSERT `s 81 (1), examples: the power is one to which s 81 applies` "power to delegate a function" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81 (1), examples: the power is one to which s 81 applies` "power to give or issue an approval, consent, licence, permit or other authority (however described)" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81 (1), examples: the power is one to which s 81 applies` "power to make an acting appointment" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81 (1), examples: the power is one to which s 81 applies` "power to issue guidelines" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81 (1), examples: the power is one to which s 81 applies` "power to repeal an Act" EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 81 (2): applies to a power to make an appointment, make a statutory instrument or do anything else in relation to an entity to be established by the authorising law.
-- s 81 (2) Example: powers under an authorising law exercised in relation to the conduct of an election for members of a board to be established as a corporation by the authorising law.
#ASSERT `s 81 (2): s 81 applies to the power to make an appointment, make a statutory instrument or do anything else in relation to the entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81 (2): s 81 applies to the power to make an appointment, make a statutory instrument or do anything else in relation to the entity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 81 (3), (4), (5): the power may be exercised at any time; the laws are taken to be in force; anything else may be done to bring the law into operation.
#ASSERT `s 81 (3): the power may be exercised at any time even though the authorising law is not in force` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81 (3): the power may be exercised at any time even though the authorising law is not in force` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 81 (4): the authorising law is taken to be in force at the time of the exercise of the power` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81 (4): the authorising law is taken to be in force at the time of the exercise of the power` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 81 (5): anything else may be done under the power at any time for the purpose of bringing the authorising law into operation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 81 (5): anything else may be done under the power at any time for the purpose of bringing the authorising law into operation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 81 (8): for a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, being notified means being made or, if approval is required, being approved.
#ASSERT `s 81 (8): the day a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument is taken to be notified` (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 3 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 81 (8): the day a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument is taken to be notified` (Date 3 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
